": ["You're right. Based on what you showed, there are **two concrete things to attack first**, and we don't need to theorize beyond them:\n\n1. **Your PowerShell startup/profile is loading extra environment/config that is bogging down every terminal.**\n2. **OpenCode is resolving `rg.exe` from `.kimi-code\\bin` even though you're not running Kimi.** That is a tooling-path contamination issue until proven otherwise.\n\nSo strip this down in the right order.\n\n### First: prove the PowerShell profile is the problem\n\nOpen a fresh terminal **without loading any PowerShell profile**:\n\n```powershell\npowershell.exe -NoProfile\n```\n\nDo nothing else in it for a moment. If that terminal is immediately responsive while your normal PowerShell is freezing, we have isolated the profile/startup layer.\n\nThen, **from that `-NoProfile` shell**, run:\n\n```powershell\n$PROFILE | Format-List *\n```\n\nand:\n\n```powershell\n@(\n  $PROFILE.AllUsersAllHosts\n  $PROFILE.AllUsersCurrentHost\n  $PROFILE.CurrentUserAllHosts\n  $PROFILE.CurrentUserCurrentHost\n) | ForEach-Object {\n  [pscustomobject]@{\n    Path = $_\n    Exists = Test-Path $_\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDo **not edit anything yet**.\n\n### Second: show exactly why `.kimi-code\\bin\\rg.exe` wins\n\nStill from `powershell.exe -NoProfile`:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Command rg -All | Select-Object CommandType,Name,Source,Definition\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\n$env:PATH -split ';' | Where-Object {\n  $_ -match 'kimi|opencode|bun|gce|node'\n}\n```\n\nThat tells us whether `.kimi-code\\bin` has been injected into the global/user PATH or by the normal PowerShell profile.\n\nAnd check the process environment indirectly with:\n\n```powershell\nwhere.exe rg\n```\n\nIf the first result is:\n\n```text\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\.kimi-code\\bin\\rg.exe\n```\n\nthen you're absolutely right: **Kimi's tool installation is supplying a generic system utility to unrelated OpenCode/Space Bunny sessions.**\n\n### The fix we are looking for\n\nNot deleting Kimi. Not killing random processes.\n\nWe want to end up with:\n\n```text\nNormal PowerShell\n    ↓\nclean lightweight profile\n\nOpenCode\n    ↓\nneutral/common rg.exe\n    ↓\nbounded active workspace\n\nKimi runtime\n    ↓\nKimi-specific tooling only when Kimi is actually invoked\n```\n\n`.kimi-code\\bin` should **not** be globally furnishing `rg.exe` to Space Bunny unless we deliberately chose that architecture.\n\nRun those checks from the **`-NoProfile` terminal**. That will separate the two problems immediately: whether the PowerShell profile is injecting the junk, and whether `.kimi-code` has contaminated the broader PATH."]}, "create_time": 1790400568.389598, "end_turn": true, "id": "40fb3fa7-78ff-4475-8f6e-99d53cb0961a", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "nedat3", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "ssatvl", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "3pln3d", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "gwnycz", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "10m1eo", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "5": {"edited": false, "id": "b7pjge", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "6": {"edited": false, "id": "z3ghqk", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "7": {"edited": false, "id": "sd44d4", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "4dfb8ef1-42c5-4e6f-8d32-0df29fe55003", "request_id": "5fbe46ef-2b52-4390-9902-35ab7004fc74", "resolved_mod