rnance Owner: Coda\\r\\nStatus: CURRENT / CANONICAL\\r\\nScope: Daily session anchoring, session continuity, human context framing, routing handoff metadata\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDefine the current canonical GCE Session Header / Footer framework used when a substantive GCE conversation or workstream is resumed or begun for a new calendar day.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis V3 standard replaces the prior separate Session Header Standard (2026-09-07) and Session Footer Standard (2026-09-07) as the current operating standard. Historical documents remain provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE DOCTRINE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA new day creates a new SESSION FRAME, not a new THREAD.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Session Frame is the daily automated anchor:\\r\\nprior accepted state / prior footer / current authoritative anchor\\r\\n→ new-day Session Header\\r\\n→ today's work\\r\\n→ Session Footer\\r\\n→ durable handoff / next-day input.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe thread/workstream lifecycle persists across days.\\r\\nPromotion of a different current subtopic does not reset thread lifecycle metrics.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nThe model executes; the Framework carries continuity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n1. GCE SESSION HEADER — V3\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTIMESTAMP:            <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY:            <Don unless explicitly delegated>\\r\\nPRIMARY SEAT:         <current functional seat>\\r\\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <current model/provider/runtime>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODE:                 <RECONCILIATION | IMPLEMENTATION | VERIFICATION |\\r\\n                       ARCHITECTURE | ADVISORY | RESEARCH | OPERATIONS>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT THREAD:       <stable conversation/workstream name>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      <1–2 lines describing exactly where the work currently is>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIORITY:             <HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATURITY:             <POC | DEVELOPMENT | VALIDATION |\\r\\n                       PRODUCTION-READY | PRODUCTION>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS:               <ACTIVE | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED | COMPLETE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTARTED:              <original thread/workstream timestamp>\\r\\nDAYS RUNNING:         <calculated automatically>\\r\\nACTIVE DAYS:          <calculated automatically>\\r\\nLAST ACTIVE:          <latest recorded activity timestamp>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact/ruling/state pointer>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIELD RULES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODE\\r\\nOperating posture only. It is not the conversation name.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT THREAD\\r\\nStable name of the active thread/workstream.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT CONTEXT\\r\\nShort description of the current position inside the thread.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIORITY\\r\\nHIGH / MEDIUM / LOW only.\\r\\nHIGH = primary, blocking, production-critical, or actively driven work.\\r\\nMEDIUM = important enabling work that does not displace the primary build.\\r\\nLOW = useful but safely deferrable work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATURITY\\r\\nHow mature the thing is.\\r\\nPOC / DEVELOPMENT / VALIDATION / PRODUCTION-READY / PRODUCTION.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS\\r\\nWhat is happening with it now.\\r\\nACTIVE / CHECKPOINT / BLOCKED / PARKED / COMPLETE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE\\r\\nConfidence in the current frame/state based on available evidence; not a model rating.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLIFECYCLE KPI RULES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTARTED\\r\\nOriginal thread/workstream start timestamp.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDAYS RUNNING\\r\\nCalendar days from STARTED through the current date, inclusive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE DAYS\\r\\nDistinct calendar days with recorded substantive activity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLAST ACTIVE\\r\\nMost recent recorded activity timestamp.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPromotion does not reset STARTED, DAYS RUNNING, or ACTIVE DAYS.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. HEADER APPENDIX A — DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRAW INTENT:\\r\\n<1–2 lines capturing what Don is actually saying/requesting>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\n<the concrete outcome Don is trying to achieve>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT:\\r\\n<why this matters / surrounding constraint / relevant state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Don Intent Snapshot is interpretive, not authoritative.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIts purpose is to expose the system's interpretation of Don's voice/text input before execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf Don corrects the interpretation, update the snapshot immediately.\\r\\nDo not silently promote an interpretation into canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. HEADER APPENDIX B — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\\r\\n- <one current workstream/subtopic>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARKED:\\r\\n- <workstream/subtopic>\\r\\n  State: <short current state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- <workstream/subtopic>\\r\\n  State: <short current state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOnly one item is PROMOTED / CURRENT at a time.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen focus changes:\\r\\nOLD CURRENT → PARKED\\r\\nNEW ITEM → PROMOTED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not silently flip lanes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPromotion changes current focus only.\\r\\nIt does not create a new thread and does not reset lifecycle KPIs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. DAILY SESSION FRAME ROLLOVER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOn the first substantive interaction with a continuing thread on a new calendar day:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Create a fresh V3 Session Header.\\r\\n2. Preserve durable thread state:\\r\\n   - AUTHORITY\\r\\n   - CURRENT THREAD\\r\\n   - CURRENT ANCHOR\\r\\n   - PRIORITY\\r\\n   - MATURITY\\r\\n   - STARTED\\r\\n   - DAYS RUNNING\\r\\n   - ACTIVE DAYS\\r\\n   - parked workstreams\\r\\n   - unresolved blockers\\r\\n   - accepted decisions\\r\\n   - latest handoff / route\\r\\n3. Refresh daily/session state:\\r\\n   - TIMESTAMP\\r\\n   - PRIMARY SEAT / OCCUPANT where changed\\r\\n   - MODE\\r\\n   - CURRENT CONTEXT\\r\\n   - STATUS\\r\\n   - CONFIDENCE\\r\\n   - LAST ACTIVE\\r\\n   - DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\\r\\n   - PROMOTED / CURRENT item\\r\\n4. Use the prior session footer plus the current authoritative anchor as the primary continuation inputs.\\r\\n5. Do not reconstruct current truth from model memory when a durable source exists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA new day creates a new SESSION_ID.\\r\\nIt does not create a new thread.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. GCE SESSION FOOTER — V3\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSEAT:                 <current seat>\\r\\nSESSION STATUS:       <CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED | COMPLETE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOUTCOME:\\r\\n<1–3 lines describing what materially happened>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDECISIONS:\\r\\n- <accepted decision>\\r\\n- <accepted decision>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLOCKERS:\\r\\n- <actual blocker only>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPEN ITEMS:\\r\\n- <unfinished item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ACTION:\\r\\n<one precise continuation action>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF:              <handoff ID/path or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFOOTER RULE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe core footer is deliberately lean.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIt answers:\\r\\n- What materially happened?\\r\\n- How confident are we?\\r\\n- What remains unresolved?\\r\\n- Where does the work go next?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not put Cable Car telemetry, full project state, controller state, or unrelated parked work into the core footer.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. FOOTER APPENDIX A — ROUTING / HANDOFF PACKET\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT:              <project identifier>\\r\\nWORKSTREAM:           <workstream identifier>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION_ID:           <stable daily session ID>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT_SEAT:         <seat>\\r\\nNEXT_ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\nAFTER_PASS:           <optional seat>\\r\\nFINAL_GATE:           <optional seat / Don>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGATE:                 <current gate>\\r\\nBLOCKER_ROUTE:        <seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT_ANCHOR:       <artifact/state pointer>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID:           <stable handoff ID>\\r\\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         <type>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\\r\\n<absolute local path>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIVE_HANDOFF_URL:\\r\\n<Google Drive URL if published>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\\r\\n<Drive artifact ID if available>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:\\r\\n<NONE | QUEUED | PUBLISHED | RECEIVED | ERROR>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nROUTING APPENDIX RULE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHuman session state and machine routing state are separate surfaces.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe routing appendix is machine-consumable continuation metadata.\\r\\nThe core footer remains human-readable and concise.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. HANDOFF IDENTITY MODEL\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOne handoff has one identity and may have multiple representations:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID\\r\\n    ├── LOCAL_PATH\\r\\n    ├── DRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID\\r\\n    └── DRIVE_URL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLocal and Google Drive copies are representations of the same handoff identity, not separate conceptual artifacts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCable Car transports/publishes the artifact.\\r\\nTransport destination does not determine artifact ownership.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTarget user affordance:\\r\\n[ OPEN LOCAL ]    [ OPEN DRIVE ]\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n8. KPI EXTENSION RULE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe V3 core header includes only the lifecycle KPIs:\\r\\n- DAYS RUNNING\\r\\n- ACTIVE DAYS\\r\\n- LAST ACTIVE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFuture KPI appendices may measure:\\r\\n- handoffs\\r\\n- seat transitions\\r\\n- gates passed\\r\\n- blockers\\r\\n- rework loops\\r\\n- average confidence\\r\\n- time blocked\\r\\n- high-priority aging\\r\\n- other operational telemetry\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not bloat the core header with those metrics.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n9. SUPERSESSION\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT:\\r\\nGCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDES AS CURRENT OPERATING STANDARD:\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_HEADER_STANDARD_2026-09-07\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_FOOTER_STANDARD_2026-09-07\\r\\n- session-header/footer formatting portions of earlier living bootstrap and prompt-delivery artifacts where inconsistent\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHistorical artifacts remain provenance and must not be rewritten to pretend V3 existed earlier.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhere an older artifact conflicts with V3 specifically on session header/footer structure or daily rollover behavior, V3 controls.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n10. CANONICAL SUMMARY\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHEADER = where we are.\\r\\nDON INTENT SNAPSHOT = what Don means, as interpreted for validation.\\r\\nACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD = what is current versus parked.\\r\\nFOOTER = what happened and what happens next.\\r\\nROUTING APPENDIX = how machines continue it.\\r\\nDAILY ROLLOVER = automated re-anchor without losing the thread.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND OF CURRENT CANONICAL SESSION FRAME V3\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n11. SUBORDINATE SESSION CONTROL FRAMES\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following subordinate controls are current under Session Frame V3:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_MID_FLIGHT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nPurpose: lightweight in-session re-grounding without creating a new daily anchor or thread.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nPurpose: resumable capture of completed work and continuation state after a meaningful slice, before pause/context switch/handoff/risky continuation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHierarchy:\\r\\nANCHOR / SESSION FRAME V3 = durable daily grounding\\r\\nMID-FLIGHT = lightweight re-grounding while moving\\r\\nCHECKPOINT = resumable state capture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE is mandatory in all three.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese subordinate frames do not replace V3. They inherit from it.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":2005},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa\",\"connector_name\":\"Google Drive\",\"action_name\":\"search\",\"is_sync\":false}"}, "create_time": 1790402190.480536, "end_turn": null, "id": "ea81cd90-1880-4d6f-97db-9163e1aa527f", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "invoked_plugin": {}, "invoked_resource": {"api_tool_version": "v2", "app_name": "Google Drive", "contains_mcp_source": false, "description": "Search Google Drive and return file or folder metadata. Calls without `item_type` and `page_token` retain the legacy search and optional best-effort text hydration. An explicit `image`, `document`, or `folder` item type searches exactly one metadata-only provider page; it never fetches file contents, even wi