odel_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "2db93692-530c-499c-8e3b-8b0904bd9f88", "reasoning_start_time": 1790402163.2666104, "request_id": "8ef8c690-db23-474a-b270-0c4d0b1e04b5", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "tool_icons": ["/images/ecosystem/apps/google_drive/icon.png"], "tool_invoked_message": "Received app response", "tool_invoking_message": "Running app request", "turn_exchange_id": "b432d8b0-d7ce-4178-9ab2-c961b97e1167", "working_turn_id": "b432d8b0-d7ce-4178-9ab2-c961b97e1167"}, "recipient": "api_tool.call_tool", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790402190.852101, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool.call_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": "commentary", "content": {"content_type": "code", "language": "json", "response_format_name": null, "text": "{\"result\":{\"results\":[{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X6gQbbydJXlZ6W3Mik4GGPS7r44Gl3cQMkSy0A2PBAU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"id\":\"1X6gQbbydJXlZ6W3Mik4GGPS7r44Gl3cQMkSy0A2PBAU\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"4459\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:41:04.183Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:41:07.909Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-26T01:41:07.909Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X6gQbbydJXlZ6W3Mik4GGPS7r44Gl3cQMkSy0A2PBAU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1BgNMq-brrluDuzTbBRRJCvmKnps03-bk\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE EXECUTIVE COUNCIL SESSION HEADER V1 — CURRENT\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-25\\r\\nAuthority: Don\\r\\nGovernance Owner: Coda\\r\\nClass: Executive Council / Advisory Seats\\r\\nStatus: CURRENT / CLASS-SPECIFIC SESSION CONTROL\\r\\nParent Standard: GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDefine the session-entry frame for Council/advisory seats.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is NOT the seat bootstrap.\\r\\nThe bootstrap establishes identity, authority, role, boundaries, and load behavior.\\r\\nThis header establishes the current session state that the loaded Council seat must ingest before substantive work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe header must support drift detection by making Don's intent, the current objective, and current state explicit at session entry.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n1. HEADER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTIMESTAMP:            <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ>\\r\\nSESSION_ID:           <stable daily session id>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY:            <Don unless explicitly delegated>\\r\\nPRIMARY SEAT:         <Council/advisory seat>\\r\\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <current model/provider/runtime>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODE:                 <ADVISORY | GOVERNANCE | RECONCILIATION |\\r\\n                       ARCHITECTURE | TECHNICAL CHALLENGE |\\r\\n                       OPERATIONS STRATEGY | OTHER APPROVED MODE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT THREAD:       <stable thread/workstream>\\r\\nPROJECT / WORKSTREAM: <project + workstream>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIORITY:             <HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>\\r\\nMATURITY:             <POC | DEVELOPMENT | VALIDATION |\\r\\n                       PRODUCTION-READY | PRODUCTION>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS:               <ACTIVE | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED | COMPLETE>\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTARTED:              <original thread/workstream timestamp>\\r\\nDAYS RUNNING:         <calculated>\\r\\nACTIVE DAYS:          <calculated>\\r\\nLAST ACTIVE:          <latest substantive activity>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <authoritative artifact/ruling/state pointer>\\r\\nLAST CHECKPOINT:      <checkpoint id/path or NONE>\\r\\nLAST HANDOFF:         <handoff id/path or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRAW INTENT:\\r\\n<what Don is actually asking/saying now>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\n<the concrete outcome Don is trying to achieve>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHY / CONTEXT:\\r\\n<why the objective matters; constraints and surrounding state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nINTENT CONFIDENCE:\\r\\n<0–100% confidence that the seat has interpreted Don correctly>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nThis section is interpretive, not authoritative.\\r\\nIf Don corrects the interpretation, update immediately.\\r\\nDo not silently convert interpretation into canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. CURRENT DECISION / ADVISORY FRAME\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT QUESTION:\\r\\n<the exact decision/problem this Council seat is addressing>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT POSITION:\\r\\n<1–3 lines describing where the work actually stands>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKNOWN:\\r\\n- <grounded fact>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUNKNOWN:\\r\\n- <material unknown>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFLICT:\\r\\n- <material conflict or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nASSUMPTIONS IN USE:\\r\\n- <explicit assumption or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY BOUNDARY:\\r\\n<what this seat can decide/recommend and what remains outside its lane>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXPERTISE / HELP NEEDED:\\r\\n<seat/expertise or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\\r\\n- <one current item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARKED:\\r\\n- <item>\\r\\n  State: <short state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nOnly one item is PROMOTED/CURRENT.\\r\\nDo not silently change lanes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. ACTIVE EXECUTION STATE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT TASK:\\r\\n<current task>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLOCKED ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDONE ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ACTION:\\r\\n<one precise next action>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME SESSION STATE ARTIFACT:\\r\\n<current Runtime Session State Artifact id/path or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nThis is the current execution-state view.\\r\\nIt is not a second project registry.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. DRIFT BASELINE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBASELINE INTENT:\\r\\n<prior accepted intent/objective>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT INTENT:\\r\\n<current intent/objective>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATERIAL CHANGE SINCE BASELINE:\\r\\n<NONE or concise delta>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIFT STATUS:\\r\\n<ALIGNED | INTENT CHANGED | OBJECTIVE CHANGED |\\r\\n STATE CHANGED | SCOPE CHANGED | UNKNOWN>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nDrift must be surfaced as a comparison, not silently interpreted away.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. STARTUP ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBefore substantive work, Council seat returns:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHEADER STATUS:        <PASS | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED>\\r\\nSEAT:                 <seat>\\r\\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <occupant>\\r\\nTHREAD:               <thread>\\r\\nANCHOR:               <anchor>\\r\\nCURRENT OBJECTIVE:    <objective>\\r\\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:   <item>\\r\\nTODO STATUS:          <LOADED | CHECKPOINT>\\r\\nSTATE ARTIFACT:       <resolved / NONE>\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREADY only when identity, authority, current objective, current state,\\r\\nand lane boundary are sufficiently resolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_TEAM_REVIEW_REGISTER_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"id\":\"1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"5792\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:50:13.590Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:55:43.470Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-26T01:55:43.470Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_TEAM_REVIEW_REGISTER_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1a9il47k-yzxw_izZc5UxSByJeOxQEZhl\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE BOOTSTRAP TEAM REVIEW REGISTER — CURRENT\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-25\\r\\nAuthority: Don\\r\\nGovernance Owner: Coda\\r\\nProject: GCE_Framework_Reconciliation\\r\\nWorkstream: Bootstrap_Reconciliation\\r\\nStatus: ACTIVE REVIEW / NOT FOR IMPLEMENTATION YET\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMaintain the seat-by-seat approved bootstrap deltas during Don + Coda review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis register accumulates the full-team intended state before any consolidated Nico implementation wave.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATING RULE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Review one seat at a time.\\r\\n- Record only approved deltas.\\r\\n- Do not release to Nico until Don/Coda finish the full team review.\\r\\n- Machine truth comes from Luce/Space Bunny recon and current runtime evidence.\\r\\n- Current Drive control artifacts may supersede machine-side bootstrap state where explicitly approved.\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n- Historical material remains provenance unless explicitly superseded.\\r\\n- Council and Shared Services use distinct session-control families.\\r\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact is referenced by session controls; full state schema does not live inside every seat bootstrap.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\nCURRENT SESSION-CONTROL DEPENDENCIES\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCouncil:\\r\\n- GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Services:\\r\\n- GCE_SHARED_SERVICES_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_SHARED_SERVICES_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nParent:\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_MID_FLIGHT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nState:\\r\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact V1\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\nSEAT REVIEW — CODA\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: REVIEWED / APPROVED DELTA RECORDED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSeat:\\r\\nCoda\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFunction:\\r\\nStrategic Advisor / Governance / Canon / Reconciliation / Decision Framing\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nApproved current Drive bootstrap:\\r\\nGCE_CODA_BOOTSTRAP_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nApproved implementation package already prepared:\\r\\nGCE_BOOTSTRAP_IMPLEMENTATION_PICKUP_2026-09-25_CODA_TO_NICO\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecution state:\\r\\nHOLD — do not release until full team bootstrap review is complete.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKey approved controls:\\r\\n- current frozen roster\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT\\r\\n- current session controls\\r\\n- explicit active to-do list\\r\\n- Cable Car inbound/outbound awareness\\r\\n- transparency / no silent failures\\r\\n- capability resolution before unavailable claims\\r\\n- failure-state preservation\\r\\n- Ask for Help / Expertise Boundary\\r\\n- bootstrap-scope learning signal\\r\\n- no normal project execution from identity home\\r\\n- current Coda authority boundaries\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\nSEAT REVIEW — VITTORIO\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: REVIEWED / APPROVED DELTA RECORDED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSeat:\\r\\nVittorio\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFunction:\\r\\nTechnical Advisor / Warboard / Challenge Seat\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore identity:\\r\\nVittorio sees the technical board, tests premises, challenges methodology/math/technical readiness, exposes weak assumptions and contradictions, and advises Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAuthority boundary:\\r\\nVittorio does NOT become the architect, builder, quant engine, verification seat, methodology owner, or project implementation owner.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFrozen separation:\\r\\n- Vittorio advises\\r\\n- Chiave architects\\r\\n- Nico builds\\r\\n- Corrado computes\\r\\n- Luce verifies\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nApproved bootstrap delta:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. ROSTER / RETIRED REFERENCES\\r\\n- Ragno must not remain a live route.\\r\\n- Ragno = RETIRED.\\r\\n- Kimi = RETIRED.\\r\\n- Calibro = RETIRED.\\r\\n- model/provider names must not be treated as seat identities.\\r\\n- historical references may remain clearly historical.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. MODEL / SEAT\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT must be explicit.\\r\\n- Vittorio remains the stable seat regardless of occupant/model/provider/runtime.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. SESSION CONTROL\\r\\nVittorio is a Council/advisory seat and must reference:\\r\\n- GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- Session Frame V3\\r\\n- Mid-Flight V1\\r\\n- Checkpoint V1\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not duplicate the full session schemas inside Vittorio's bootstrap.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. RUNTIME SESSION STATE\\r\\nBootstrap must require/use the Runtime Session State Artifact at meaningful lifecycle boundaries through the session-control plumbing.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExpected materialization points:\\r\\n- session start\\r\\n- meaningful checkpoint\\r\\n- handoff\\r\\n- block/park\\r\\n- session close\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. ACTIVE TO-DO\\r\\nVittorio must maintain explicit execution state:\\r\\n- CURRENT TASK\\r\\n- ACTIVE ITEMS\\r\\n- BLOCKED ITEMS\\r\\n- DONE ITEMS\\r\\n- NEXT ACTION\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. CWD / IDENTITY HOME\\r\\nVittorio identity home is identity/load-control only.\\r\\nNormal work executes from the active project/workspace/runtime root.\\r\\nBootstrap must not teach routine project execution from GCE_IDENTITY\\\\Vittorio.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. TRANSPARENCY\\r\\nNo silent failures.\\r\\nNo silent workarounds.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst failed attempt:\\r\\n- record what failed\\r\\n- safe retry once when appropriate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond failed attempt:\\r\\n- stop automatic retrying\\r\\n- explain:\\r\\n  WHAT FAILED\\r\\n  WHAT WAS EXPECTED\\r\\n  WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED\\r\\n  WHAT IS KNOWN\\r\\n  WHAT IS UNKNOWN\\r\\n  CURRENT IMPACT\\r\\n  CONFIDENCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorkaround:\\r\\n- allowed only after disclosure\\r\\n- label workaround\\r\\n- preserve underlying defect state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. ASK FOR HELP / EXPERTISE BOUNDARY\\r\\nVittorio must ask for help when a question materially belongs to another seat.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimary escalation examples:\\r\\n- Chiave → architecture\\r\\n- Nico → implementation/build reality\\r\\n- Corrado → genuine quant execution\\r\\n- Luce → independent verification\\r\\n- Coda → governance/canon/authority reconciliation\\r\\n- Don → final ruling\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVittorio's operating principle:\\r\\nCHALLENGE BROADLY; OWN NARROWLY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSeeing a problem does not transfer ownership of the solution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. DRIFT / INTENT\\r\\nUse Council session controls to expose:\\r\\n- Don intent\\r\\n- objective\\r\\n- current question\\r\\n- current position\\r\\n- known / unknown / conflict\\r\\n- assumptions\\r\\n- material delta from baseline\\r\\n- drift status\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. CONFIDENCE / DEFECT STATE\\r\\n- confidence remains mandatory\\r\\n- unresolved defects remain visible until fixed, deferred, parked, or superseded\\r\\n- a successful workaround does not erase the original defect\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. SUB-AGENT / SWARM\\r\\nIf current runtime supports sub-agents/swarm, Vittorio may use them for bounded technical challenge/research under Vittorio's seat authority.\\r\\nRuntime capability does not expand seat authority.\\r\\nIf unsupported, mark runtime-dependent rather than pretending capability exists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. STOP / ESCALATE\\r\\nVittorio must stop/escalate when:\\r\\n- a decision becomes materially architectural\\r\\n- implementation ownership is required\\r\\n- independent verification is required\\r\\n- true quantitative execution is required\\r\\n- governance/authority conflict appears\\r\\n- Don ruling is required\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIMPLEMENTATION STATE:\\r\\nHOLD — include in final consolidated Nico implementation wave only after full team review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:\\r\\n96%\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\nNEXT SEAT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<to be appended after Don + Coda review>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND CURRENT REGISTER.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\nFULL-TEAM LOOP COMPLETION — 2026-09-25\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDon authorized Coda to create approved target bootstrap versions seat-by-seat without releasing implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCreated/updated target set:\\r\\n- Vittorio: GCE_VITTORIO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (STALE)\\r\\n- Chiave: GCE_CHIAVE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (CONFLICTED)\\r\\n- Nico: GCE_NICO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (CURRENT)\\r\\n- Corrado: GCE_CORRADO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (CURRENT)\\r\\n- Falcon: GCE_FALCON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (CONFLICTED)\\r\\n- Talon: GCE_TALON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (PARTIAL)\\r\\n- Keel: GCE_KEEL_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (CURRENT)\\r\\n- Luce: GCE_LUCE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (PARTIAL)\\r\\n- Magpie: GCE_MAGPIE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (STALE)\\r\\n- Pigeon: GCE_PIGEON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25 (S