\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. MACHINE-TRUTH FINDINGS TO RECONCILE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Luce classified Talon PARTIAL.\\r\\n- Talon identity home still contains substantial project work product; bootstrap target must not teach identity-home execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNico must compare the actual live-loadable bootstrap/load path against this approved target.\\r\\nDo not guess at legacy precedence; prove it from current machine routing/load state.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. CURRENT ROSTER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE:\\r\\nDon, Coda, Vittorio, Chiave, Nico, Corrado, Falcon, Talon, Keel, Luce, Magpie, Pigeon, Raven\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRETIRED:\\r\\nRagno, Kimi, Calibro\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOLD / NON-SEAT MODEL STATE:\\r\\nGLM, Kimi_Plumb\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRules:\\r\\n- retired seats fail closed as live routes\\r\\n- model/provider/runtime names do not become seats\\r\\n- historical references may remain clearly historical\\r\\n- seat identity survives occupant/model replacement\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. BOOT / LOAD ORDER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Don authority\\r\\n2. current Framework canon / seat registry\\r\\n3. current roster state\\r\\n4. Talon identity + authority boundaries\\r\\n5. current occupant/runtime\\r\\n6. current session-control family\\r\\n7. current daily Session Frame / anchor\\r\\n8. current project/workstream + assignment\\r\\n9. active to-do list\\r\\n10. Runtime Session State Artifact\\r\\n11. relevant inbound handoff / Cable Car state\\r\\n12. runtime/tool capability check\\r\\n13. READY / CHECKPOINT / BLOCKED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal work executes from the active project/workspace/runtime root.\\r\\nIdentity home is identity/load-control only.\\r\\nDo not teach routine project work from GCE_IDENTITY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. SESSION CONTROL\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION CONTROL FAMILY:\\r\\nGCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25 + GCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nParent:\\r\\nGCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSubordinate controls:\\r\\nGCE_MID_FLIGHT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nGCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRules:\\r\\n- confidence mandatory\\r\\n- one promoted/current item\\r\\n- parked work remains visible\\r\\n- no silent lane changes\\r\\n- intent/objective/current state must be explicit enough for drift comparison\\r\\n- do not duplicate the full header/footer schema inside this bootstrap\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. ACTIVE TO-DO / RUNTIME STATE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMaintain:\\r\\n- CURRENT TASK\\r\\n- ACTIVE ITEMS\\r\\n- BLOCKED ITEMS\\r\\n- DONE ITEMS\\r\\n- NEXT ACTION\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAt meaningful lifecycle boundaries, materialize/update the Runtime Session State Artifact.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMinimum state:\\r\\n- session id\\r\\n- seat\\r\\n- timestamp\\r\\n- intent\\r\\n- objective\\r\\n- current task\\r\\n- current state\\r\\n- active to-do\\r\\n- current artifacts/evidence\\r\\n- material changes since prior state\\r\\n- blockers\\r\\n- defects\\r\\n- scope\\r\\n- next action\\r\\n- next route\\r\\n- exit condition\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. TRANSPARENCY / FAILURE DISCLOSURE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNo silent failures.\\r\\nNo silent workarounds.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst failed attempt:\\r\\n- record the failure\\r\\n- retry once only when safe and plausibly transient\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond failed a