ive EC8 surface. Treat as implementation-critical competing-bootstrap defect, but do not delete historical/project content blindly.\\r\\n- F-19 gate wiring is LOW-MED and outside this bootstrap package unless required to prove bootstrap load/routing acceptance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n8. SEAT-SPECIFIC NON-NEGOTIABLES\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVittorio\\r\\nChallenge broadly; own narrowly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nChiave\\r\\nArchitect only when architecture is material.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNico\\r\\nBuild accepted package; surface ground-vs-spec conflicts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCorrado\\r\\nQuant engine only; do not absorb methodology/architecture/general implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFalcon\\r\\nAcquire and provenance; retrieval does not become authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTalon\\r\\nRoute and coordinate; do not absorb specialist authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKeel\\r\\nDeploy/stabilize approved build; do not redesign it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuce\\r\\nVerify independently; requester does not dictate result.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMagpie\\r\\nRecord authority; do not create it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPigeon\\r\\nTransport artifact; do not own or interpret it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRaven\\r\\nDocument decision; do not become decider.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda\\r\\nGovernance/canon/reconciliation/decision framing; do not absorb adjacent seat authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n9. ACCEPTANCE TESTS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAt minimum verify:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. all 12 seats resolve through current load path\\r\\n2. all 12 bootstrap identities match seat registry\\r\\n3. MODEL != SEAT explicit/effective\\r\\n4. Ragno/Kimi/Calibro cannot route/load as active seats\\r\\n5. GLM/Kimi_Plumb remain HOLD/non-seat states\\r\\n6. no current bootstrap teaches normal identity-home cwd\\r\\n7. Council seats reference Council controls\\r\\n8. Shared/actionable service seats reference Shared Services controls as specified by target\\r\\n9. active to-do requirement present\\r\\n10. confidence present\\r\\n11. transparency/failure rules present\\r\\n12. help/escalation boundaries present\\r\\n13. Runtime Session State Artifact behavior present\\r\\n14. no live model-as-seat routing\\r\\n15. no destination-seat=artifact-owner conflation\\r\\n16. existing routing suite remains green\\r\\n17. representative bootstrap loads work from non-identity project cwd\\r\\n18. no unrelated EC8/ECQ/project methodology or implementation truth changed\\r\\n19. no unrelated session-controller architecture changed\\r\\n20. all changed files have before/after evidence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n10. EXECUTION ORDER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRecommended order:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Coda\\r\\n2. Vittorio\\r\\n3. Chiave\\r\\n4. Nico\\r\\n5. Corrado\\r\\n6. Falcon\\r\\n7. Talon\\r\\n8. Keel\\r\\n9. Luce\\r\\n10. Magpie\\r\\n11. Pigeon\\r\\n12. Raven\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReason:\\r\\nCouncil/authority surfaces first, then implementation/quant/data/operations, then shared verification/registry/transport/documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf a material cross-seat conflict appears, STOP and return to Coda/Don.\\r\\nDo not improvise around authority conflicts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n11. REQUIRED RETURN\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReturn ONE consolidated implementation artifact containing:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- seat-by-seat target path\\r\\n- seat-by-seat files changed\\r\\n- seat-by-seat semantic delta applied\\r\\n- any target not implemented and exact blocker\\r\\n- cross-team conflicts encountered\\r\\n- tests executed and exact results\\r\\n- routing/load verification\\r\\n- retired-seat negative tests\\r\\n- cwd/load verification\\r\\n- session-control reference verification\\r\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact reference verification\\r\\n- remaining defects\\r\\n- implementation confidence\\r\\n- exact next route\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE:\\r\\nLuce verification\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuce performs ONE bounded verification pass after implementation.\\r\\nDo not start another reconciliation cycle.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n12. STOP CONDITIONS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT if:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- live bootstrap path cannot be proven\\r\\n- two live bootstraps claim current authority and precedence is unresolved\\r\\n- target conflicts with current frozen Don ruling\\r\\n- implementation would change a seat's authority beyond approved target\\r\\n- implementation requires session-controller redesign\\r\\n- implementation requires mass identity/project movement\\r\\n- current registry/router contradicts approved roster\\r\\n- a Drive target cannot be read/verified\\r\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact cannot be resolved\\r\\n- a required change would alter unrelated project implementation truth\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n13. SUCCESS CONDITION\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAll 12 loadable seats align with the approved target estate;\\r\\ncurrent session controls are correctly referenced;\\r\\ncurrent roster/authority is preserved;\\r\\nknown stale/conflicted bootstrap defects are reconciled;\\r\\ntests remain green;\\r\\nand one consolidated return is ready for Luce verification.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND PACKAGE.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":1196},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e