dk\",\"title\":\"GCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"id\":\"1Z5Nd-36296q6oc8xJRSrrGlRyBvhoupELQ04mR1gm3U\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"4178\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T00:20:52.325Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T00:22:04.871Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-26T00:22:04.871Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Z5Nd-36296q6oc8xJRSrrGlRyBvhoupELQ04mR1gm3U/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1BgNMq-brrluDuzTbBRRJCvmKnps03-bk\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE CHECKPOINT FRAME V1 — CURRENT\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-25\\r\\nAuthority: Don\\r\\nGovernance Owner: Coda\\r\\nParent Standard: GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nStatus: CURRENT / SUBORDINATE SESSION CONTROL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCapture a resumable, confidence-bearing state after a meaningful slice of work, before a pause, context switch, handoff, or potentially risky continuation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA Checkpoint is heavier than Mid-Flight and lighter than a full Anchor.\\r\\nIt summarizes what was accomplished from the current anchor and what must be preserved to resume safely.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE RULE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR = durable daily grounding.\\r\\nMID-FLIGHT = lightweight re-grounding while moving.\\r\\nCHECKPOINT = resumable capture of completed work and continuation state.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA checkpoint does not automatically create a new daily anchor.\\r\\nCONFIDENCE is mandatory.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n1. GCE CHECKPOINT HEADER — V1\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTIMESTAMP:            <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARENT ANCHOR:        <current V3 daily anchor>\\r\\nAUTHORITY:            Don\\r\\nPRIMARY SEAT:         <seat>\\r\\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <model/runtime>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODE:                 <current operating mode>\\r\\nCURRENT THREAD:       <stable thread name>\\r\\nCHECKPOINT SUBJECT:   <what is being checkpointed>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIORITY:             <HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>\\r\\nSTATUS:               CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT CONTEXT:\\r\\n<1–2 lines describing where the session stands at checkpoint time>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ANCHOR:\\r\\n<authoritative state/artifact governing the work>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. HEADER APPENDIX — CHECKPOINT BASIS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON INTENT:\\r\\n<what Don intended this slice to accomplish>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHECKPOINT REASON:\\r\\n<PAUSE | CONTEXT SWITCH | HANDOFF | VALIDATION | BEFORE RISKY STEP | MANUAL>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSCOPE SINCE LAST MARKER:\\r\\n<short bounded description of work covered by this checkpoint>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT CHANGE:\\r\\n<NONE or what changed since the parent anchor / previous marker>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. GCE CHECKPOINT FOOTER — V1\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS:               <PROCEED | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED | COMPLETE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOUTCOME:\\r\\n<2–4 lines describing what is now materially true>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCOMPLETED:\\r\\n- <completed item>\\r\\n- <completed item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDECISIONS:\\r\\n- <accepted decision>\\r\\n- NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nARTIFACTS / STATE CHANGED:\\r\\n- <real artifact or state>\\r\\n- NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLOCKERS:\\r\\n- <actual blocker>\\r\\n- NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPEN ITEMS:\\r\\n- <unfinished item>\\r\\n- NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ACTION:\\r\\n<one precise continuation step>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR IMPACT:\\r\\n<NONE | UPDATE REQUIRED | NEW ANCHOR REQUIRED>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF:\\r\\n<NONE | handoff ID/path>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. FOOTER APPENDIX — RESUME PACKET\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARENT ANCHOR:        <current daily anchor>\\r\\nCHECKPOINT ID:        <stable checkpoint ID>\\r\\nCURRENT SEAT:         <seat>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\\r\\n<current workstream/subtopic>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARKED:\\r\\n<only items materially relevant to resumption, or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLAST VERIFIED STATE:\\r\\n<short statement of last verified / accepted state>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRESUME FROM:\\r\\n<exact next step, artifact, question, or command>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE:\\r\\n<seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLOCKER ROUTE:\\r\\n<seat / Don / NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:\\r\\n<0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- A Checkpoint must preserve enough state to resume without reconstructing the session from memory.\\r\\n- COMPLETED means actually completed, not proposed.\\r\\n- ARTIFACTS / STATE CHANGED names only real changes.\\r\\n- DECISIONS lists only accepted decisions.\\r\\n- If a required correction must occur before continuation, STATUS is CHECKPOINT or BLOCKED, not PROCEED.\\r\\n- ANCHOR IMPACT distinguishes whether the daily anchor must change.\\r\\n- The Resume Packet is the compact continuation payload for the same chat, another seat, or a later return.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. TRIGGER RULE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA Checkpoint Frame may be triggered when Don explicitly says:\\r\\n- checkpoint\\r\\n- pause here\\r\\n- save our place\\r\\n- before we switch\\r\\n- summarize what we just did\\r\\n- hand this off\\r\\n- capture this before continuing\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA checkpoint may also be appropriate before:\\r\\n- a material context switch\\r\\n- a handoff\\r\\n- a risky implementation step\\r\\n- a long pause\\r\\n- session compaction / context pressure\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA checkpoint is not automatically a session close.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":1347},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa\",\"connector_name\":\"Google Drive\",\"action_name\":\"search\",\"is_sync\":false}"}, "create_time": 1790402199.418549, "end_turn": null, "id": "e7a7d343-95b0-4a31-b460-131bff055824", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "invoked_plugin": {}, "invoked_resource": {"api_tool_version": "v2", "app_name": "Google Drive", "contains_mcp_source": false, "description": "Search Google Drive and return file or folder metadata. Calls without `item_type` and `page_token` retain the legacy search and optional best-effort text hydration. An explicit `image`, `document`, or `folder` item type searches exactly one metadata-only provider page; it never fetches file contents, even with `best_effort_fetch=True`. Return the opaque, provider-owned `next_page_token` unchanged as the next request's `page_token`, including when a page has no allowed results. Use short, specific keywords, or omit the query to browse accessible files. Broaden an empty-result search with related terms, abbreviations, or synonyms. `special_filter_query_str` is a raw Google Drive v3 `q` filter for MIME type, modification time, ownership, sharing, or folder selection. Set `require_viewed_by_user=True` to restrict results to viewed files. Search covers all accessible drives by default. Do not pass unsupported `top_k`, `max_results`, `page_size`, `folder_url`, `query_type`, `user_message`, 