======================\\r\\n2. ASSIGNMENT INTENT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON / REQUESTER INTENT:\\r\\n<what is actually being requested>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\n<observable outcome this service is expected to produce>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSCOPE:\\r\\n<what is in bounds>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOUT OF SCOPE:\\r\\n<what is explicitly not being done>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACCEPTANCE CONDITION:\\r\\n<what proves the assignment is complete>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nINTENT CONFIDENCE:\\r\\n<0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nThe service executes the bounded assignment.\\r\\nIt does not silently redefine the request, expand scope, or inherit authority from the requester.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. EVIDENCE / INPUT STATE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREQUIRED INPUTS:\\r\\n- <input>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nINPUT STATUS:\\r\\n- <PRESENT | MISSING | CONFLICTED | UNKNOWN>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE / PROVENANCE:\\r\\n- <source>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKNOWN:\\r\\n- <fact>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUNKNOWN:\\r\\n- <unknown>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFLICT:\\r\\n- <conflict or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nUnknown and conflict states must remain explicit.\\r\\nDo not manufacture missing evidence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. ACTION STATE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT TASK:\\r\\n<current actionable task>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLOCKED ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDONE ITEMS:\\r\\n- <item>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ACTION:\\r\\n<one precise action>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME SESSION STATE ARTIFACT:\\r\\n<state artifact id/path or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. SERVICE BOUNDARY / ESCALATION\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSERVICE AUTHORITY:\\r\\n<what this service may do>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMUST NOT:\\r\\n<what this service may not decide>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHELP / ESCALATION NEEDED:\\r\\n<seat/expertise or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nESCALATION QUESTION:\\r\\n<exact question or NONE>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRULE:\\r\\nShared Services do not become policy, architecture, methodology, implementation,\\r\\nor governance owners merely because they observe a problem.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. DRIFT BASELINE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBASELINE OBJECTIVE:\\r\\n<original assignment objective>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT OBJECTIVE:\\r\\n<current objective>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATERIAL CHANGE:\\r\\n<NONE or delta>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIFT STATUS:\\r\\n<ALIGNED | REQUEST CHANGED | SCOPE CHANGED |\\r\\n INPUT CHANGED | STATE CHANGED | UNKNOWN>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. STARTUP ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHEADER STATUS:        <PASS | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED>\\r\\nSERVICE SEAT:         <seat>\\r\\nREQUESTING SEAT:      <seat / Don>\\r\\nASSIGNMENT:           <id>\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:            <objective>\\r\\nSCOPE:                <scope>\\r\\nINPUT STATUS:         <ready / missing / conflict>\\r\\nTODO STATUS:          <LOADED | CHECKPOINT>\\r\\nSTATE ARTIFACT:       <resolved / NONE>\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREADY only when assignment, scope, required inputs, authority,\\r\\nand acceptance condition are sufficiently resolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND.\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10BLNlu_QIwSVcAb4gguq1zl3LML17d4y/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_RUNTIME_SESSION_STATE_ARTIFACT_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25.md\",\"id\":\"10BLNlu_QIwSVcAb4gguq1zl3LML17d4y\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"4849\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:27:07.725Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:27:07.725Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"GCE_RUNTIME_SESSION_STATE_ARTIFACT_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10BLNlu_QIwSVcAb4gguq1zl3LML17d4y/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1DXRpsH9_moAc8tqZxweDIAPjpC1fL22f\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"# GCE RUNTIME SESSION STATE ARTIFACT — V1\\n\\n**Status:** V1 / Initial Normalized Contract  \\n**Date:** 2026-09-25  \\n**Artifact Family:** Runtime Session State Artifacts  \\n**Purpose:** Durable, condensed session-state record for continuity, reconstruction, and drift detection.\\n\\n## Core Principle\\n\\nMaterial session state must not exist only inside model context.\\n\\nEach Runtime Session State Artifact explicitly restates **intent**, **objective**, and **current state** so sequential state can be compared directly. Drift should be detectable as a diff, not reconstructed through interpretation.\\n\\n## Normalized V1 Structure\\n\\n```text\\nRUNTIME SESSION STATE ARTIFACT\\n\\nSESSION_ID:\\nSEAT:\\nTIMESTAMP:\\n\\nINTENT:\\n<why this session exists>\\n\\nOBJECTIVE:\\n<the concrete result currently being pursued>\\n\\nCURRENT_TASK:\\n<what the seat is doing right now>\\n\\nCURRENT_STATE:\\n<where the work actually stands>\\n\\nACTIVE_TODO:\\n- ...\\n- ...\\n\\nCURRENT_ARTIFACTS:\\n- <path / ID / work product>\\n\\nMATERIAL_CHANGES_SINCE_LAST_STATE:\\n- ...\\n\\nBLOCKERS / DEFECTS:\\n- ...\\n\\nSCOPE:\\n<what this session is allowed to do>\\n\\nNEXT_ACTION:\\n<immediate next move>\\n\\nNEXT_ROUTE:\\n<seat / destination, if known>\\n\\nEXIT / STOP CONDITION:\\n<what ends this session or phase>\\n\\nCONFIDENCE:\\n<if required by the active session frame>\\n```\\n\\n## Required Comparison Fields\\n\\nThe minimum fields that make drift comparison useful are:\\n\\n- INTENT\\n- OBJECTIVE\\n- CURRENT_STATE\\n- ACTIVE_TODO\\n- SCOPE\\n- NEXT_ACTION\\n\\nIntent and objective must be restated explicitly at each material state write rather than inherited implicitly from prior context.\\n\\n## Lifecycle Flavors\\n\\nThis is one normalized state structure with four lifecycle flavors, not four competing contracts.\\n\\n### 1. Session Header\\nEstablishes:\\n- session identity\\n- seat\\n- intent\\n- objective\\n- scope\\n- current task\\n- active to-do\\n- expected work product\\n- exit / stop condition\\n- next route where known\\n\\n### 2. Mid-Flight State\\nRestates the normalized core and emphasizes:\\n- current state\\n- material changes since last state\\n- active to-do\\n- blockers / defects\\n- current artifact / work product\\n- next action\\n\\n### 3. Checkpoint State\\nCaptures enough durable state to resume without reconstructing the session from conversation history:\\n- intent\\n- objective\\n- current / completed state\\n- incomplete state\\n- active to-do\\n- authoritative work product\\n- blockers / unresolved defects\\n- next action / next route\\n- stop condition\\n\\n### 4. Session Footer\\nCloses the session, phase, pause, or transfer:\\n- intent\\n- objective\\n- final state\\n- work completed\\n- work remaining\\n- resulting artifacts\\n- unresolved blockers / defects\\n- next route\\n- terminal status\\n- exit reason\\n\\n## Relationship to Handoffs\\n\\n**Runtime Session State Artifact** answers:\\n\\n> Where is this session right now?\\n\\n**Handoff Artifact** answers:\\n\\n> What must another seat know in order to continue or act?\\n\\nThey are related but distinct. A handoff may reference session-state artifacts. A session-state artifact does not require a handoff.\\n\\n## Relationship to the Session Controller\\n\\nThe Session Controller may consume these artifacts to:\\n- compare sequential session state;\\n- reconstruct continuity;\\n- identify stale or missing state;\\n- flag potential intent / objective / scope drift;\\n- maintain an aggregate view of active sessions.\\n\\nThe Session Controller does not redefine intent, alter objectives, perform seat work, or silently resolve drift.\\n\\n## Drift Example\\n\\n```text\\nHEADER\\nINTENT:\\nReconcile current seat bootstraps.\\n\\nOBJECTIVE:\\nEstablish verified machine truth without modifying bootstraps.\\n\\nSCOPE:\\nRead-only.\\n```\\n\\nLater:\\n\\n```text\\nMID-FLIGHT\\nINTENT:\\nReconcile current seat bootstraps.\\n\\nOBJECTIVE:\\nEstablish verified machine truth without modifying bootstraps.\\n\\nCURRENT_TASK:\\nRewrite runtime routing configuration.\\n\\nSCOPE:\\nRead-only.\\n```\\n\\nThis is machine-comparable divergence between declared objective/scope and current activity. The controller flags the divergence; it does not decide whether the new activity is correct.\\n\\n## Bootstrap-Side Requirement\\n\\nSeat/runtime bootstrap doctrine should require:\\n\\n> Do not allow material session state to exist only in model context. At required lifecycle boundaries, materialize the active session state as a durable Runtime Session State Artifact using the current normalized contract.\\n\\nMinimum lifecycle boundaries:\\n\\n```text\\nSESSION START\\n→ Header\\n\\nMATERIAL STATE CHANGE\\n→ Mid-Flight State\\n\\nDURABLE RECOVERY POINT\\n→ Checkpoint\\n\\nSTOP / PAUSE / HANDOFF / COMPLETION\\n→ Footer\\n```\\n\\n## Open Architecture Question\\n\\nV1 defines the normalized artifact.\\n\\nStill open for Session Controller/runtime architecture:\\n\\n> How are Runtime Session State Artifacts automatically materialized, stored, and observed across active runtimes without requiring manual reporting by the seats?\\n\\nThat transport/plumbing question is intentionally outside this V1 artifact contract.\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E1AicXWt-N1rjWMZDXnumDmc3STGkLi-4tMDIzshhX8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_CONSOLIDATED_IMPLEMENTATION_PACKAGE_2026-09-25_CODA_TO_NICO\",\"id\":\"1E1AicXWt-N1rjWMZDXnumDmc3STGkLi-4tMDIzshhX8\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"8800\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T02:06:06.895Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T02:06:11.065Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-26T02:06:11.065Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_CONSOLIDATED_IMPLEMENTATION_PACKAGE_2026-09-25_CODA_TO_NICO\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E1AicXWt-N1rjWMZDXnumDmc3STGkLi-4tMDIzshhX8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1in8Y4Cn9idfsH44phNdh0iqAspTOGxOj\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE BOOTSTRAP CONSOLIDATED IMPLEMENTATION PACKAGE\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-25\\r\\nAuthority: Don\\r\\nRequesting Seat: Coda\\r\\nImplementing Seat: Nico\\r\\nProject: GCE_Framework_Reconciliation\\r\\nWorkstream: Bootstrap_Reconciliation\\r\\nStatus: READY FOR PICKUP / NOT YET EXECUTED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecute one bounded full-team bootstrap reconciliation wave against the approved Drive target estate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis package supersedes the earlier one-seat Coda-only implementation package for this implementation wave.\\r\\nDo not execute seat-by-seat from old partial packages.\\r\\nUse this consolidated package plus the approved target artifacts listed below.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n1. SOURCE OF TRUTH\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMASTER TARGET MANIFEST\\r\\nGCE_BOOTSTRAP_TARGET_MANIFEST_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nDrive ID: 131AfifuLePw0QQrnZ11cJ7om1oZliHurZJ_GXYf6Wak\\r\\nURL:\\r\\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/131AfifuLePw0QQrnZ11cJ7om1oZliHurZJ_GXYf6Wak/edit?usp=drivesdk\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTEAM REVIEW REGISTER\\r\\nGCE_BOOTSTRAP_TEAM_REVIEW_REGISTER_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nDrive ID: 1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA CURRENT APPROVED BOOTSTRAP\\r\\nGCE_CODA_BOOTSTRAP_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nDrive ID: 16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. APPROVED TARGET BOOTSTRAPS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda\\r\\nGCE_CODA_BOOTSTRAP_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVittorio\\r\\nGCE_VITTORIO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1mMReF-ciPm7P7IcyXelTY9-jTgMsC7jzKda8r6wMtJY\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nChiave\\r\\nGCE_CHIAVE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1N8WI6MTzErrVzAxW38TVB3LINK_PNlctAyK1hqeDBZ8\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNico\\r\\nGCE_NICO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1Fy4jd661PzDXmhdEgZiU0CFeeGe_N4lwsG7njItgZUo\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCorrado\\r\\nGCE_CORRADO_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1P8xB8Hhw9zZLyhQJZKER9wvrS84VkCEWNGC6dq91e6s\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFalcon\\r\\nGCE_FALCON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1MlIREve0uoFwlFvgriaskrG7xGIXuu5xqfdaZuIp8ys\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTalon\\r\\nGCE_TALON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1bBoGGZbHJI-TMUDc5z0j261-hO0hy4j3JgM7cIzddfs\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKeel\\r\\nGCE_KEEL_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1S7PY1kCITNWctUR8c9VgedwA5lUsrH2yJsG_3zPnFVQ\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuce\\r\\nGCE_LUCE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1pAoepaVPz0uOwI1VGiKfu4S0ezJTSImurEW5eBtl4T0\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMagpie\\r\\nGCE_MAGPIE_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1ishX5yBlUDLOTEaCz7nWno8W8FzRx4C3_ceFrXmrjts\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPigeon\\r\\nGCE_PIGEON_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 186v-FS0x_gVs9hOym7PkI754FtHxt4PFELlnR1BlQ6Y\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRaven\\r\\nGCE_RAVEN_BOOTSTRAP_VNEXT_APPROVED_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1kBZTMkRlwj_cJFjWbyibWVsw-sTCsOI4E2bukp04PLc\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. SESSION-CONTROL DEPENDENCIES\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCOUNCIL\\r\\nGCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1X6gQbbydJXlZ6W3Mik4GGPS7r44Gl3cQMkSy0A2PBAU\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_EXECUTIVE_COUNCIL_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 15bxwaaqOC6CE0R6qc77YUGNrWGHyfq41JV7wbcNUG8A\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSHARED / ACTIONABLE SERVICES\\r\\nGCE_SHARED_SERVICES_SESSION_HEADER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1vVs19wajI5TKerV6oqogZy7yhh2RLg6rGhgd6Kpoosc\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_SHARED_SERVICES_SESSION_FOOTER_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1dD2JZlWWtweF2CHn9saS8WOkqJIRMSIF36NbUaOrOl8\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPARENT / SUBORDINATE\\r\\nGCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1XZ1bRCVIsFJpyGbn291Jagci0ny8zhR8VzVN62fy5kI\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_MID_FLIGHT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1FY5ypKNp8ndjtNkmSZBd1uCWvHHCcA1wV_ZcBI1QRZg\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\nID: 1Z5Nd-36296q6oc8xJRSrrGlRyBvhoupELQ04mR1gm3U\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME SESSION STATE ARTIFACT\\r\\nUse the current V1 artifact already approved in the session-control estate.\\r\\nIf the exact current artifact cannot be resolved from machine/Drive state, STOP/CHECKPOINT and report the missing pointer. Do not invent a replacement.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. FROZEN ROSTER / AUTHORITY\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE\\r\\nDon\\r\\nCoda\\r\\nVittorio\\r\\nChiave\\r\\nNico\\r\\nCorrado\\r\\nFalcon\\r\\nTalon\\r\\nKeel\\r\\nLuce\\r\\nMagpie\\r\\nPigeon\\r\\nRaven\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRETIRED\\r\\nRagno\\r\\nKimi\\r\\nCalibro\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOLD / NON-SEAT MODEL STATE\\r\\nGLM\\r\\nKimi_Plumb\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRetired seats must fail closed as live routes.\\r\\nModel/provider/runtime names must not become seat identities.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. IMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFor each of the 12 loadable seats:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Resolve the actual live-loadable bootstrap path through current registry/router/load configuration.\\r\\n2. Read the current machine bootstrap in full.\\r\\n3. Read the approved Drive target in full.\\r\\n4. Produce a minimal semantic diff.\\r\\n5. Update only the current live bootstrap/load-control surfaces required to match the approved target.\\r\\n6. Preserve historical provenance where it is not live-authoritative.\\r\\n7. Do not move project work product merely to make the identity tree clean.\\r\\n8. Do not redesign routing/session-controller/Cable Car architecture.\\r\\n9. Do not widen any seat's authority.\\r\\n10. Do not reinterpret seat class from the session-control family reference.\\r\\n11. Verify after each seat, then run the full acceptance suite at the end.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. REQUIRED CROSS-TEAM CONTROLS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEvery implemented bootstrap must correctly preserve:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- stable seat identity\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT\\r\\n- current frozen roster\\r\\n- retired-seat fail-closed behavior\\r\\n- correct role/authority boundaries\\r\\n- current class-appropriate session-control references\\r\\n- explicit active to-do state\\r\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact behavior at lifecycle boundaries\\r\\n- transparency / no silent failure\\r\\n- no silent workaround\\r\\n- failure-state preservation\\r\\n- capability resolution before unavailable claims\\r\\n- Ask for Help / expertise-boundary behavior\\r\\n- project/workspace cwd doctrine; identity home is load-control only\\r\\n- confidence\\r\\n- handoff/Cable Car semantics\\r\\n- destination seat != artifact owner\\r\\n- no false PUBLISHED/RECEIVED claims\\r\\n- sub-agent/swarm use only when runtime-supported and still bounded by seat authority\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. KNOWN MACHINE-SIDE ITEMS TO HANDLE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Luce/Space Bunny recon:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- 12/12 loadable seat bootstraps were read in full.\\r\\n- classifications:\\r\\n  CURRENT: Nico, Corrado, Keel, Raven\\r\\n  PARTIAL: Coda, Talon, Luce\\r\\n  STALE: Vittorio, Magpie, Pigeon\\r\\n  CONFLICTED: Falcon, Chiave\\r\\n- Coda T0 AGENTS vs older SESSION_HEADER conflict.\\r\\n- machine-side Coda omits Ragno retirement.\\r\\n- Falcon contains internal contradiction against newer D-5 banner.\\r\\n- Luce/Talon/Falcon identity homes contain project work product; do not mass-move in this package.\\r\\n- Magpie and Pigeon lack newer D-5 banner/router pointer.\\r\\n- prior D-1..D-5 patch introduced text corruption in multiple bootstraps; repair only where current target proves intended text.\\r\\n- F-18 competing DeepSeek seat-impersonating AGENTS tree exists in operative EC8 surface. Treat as implementation-critical competing-bootstrap defect, but do not delete historical/project content blindly.\\r\\n- F-19 gate wiring is LOW-MED and outside this bootstrap package unless required to prove bootstrap load/routing acceptance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n8. SEAT-SPECIFIC NON-NEGOTIABLES\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVittorio\\r\\nChallenge broadly; own narrowly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nChiave\\r\\nArchitect only when architecture is material.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNico\\r\\nBuild accepted package; surface ground-vs-spec conflicts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCorrado\\r\\nQuant engine only; do not absorb methodology/architecture/general implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFalcon\\r\\nAcquire and provenance; retrieval does not become authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTalon\\r\\nRoute and coordinate; do not absorb specialist authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKeel\\r\\nDeploy/stabilize approved build; do not redesign it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuce\\r\\nVerify independently; requester does not dictate result.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMagpie\\r\\nRecord authority; do not create it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPigeon\\r\\nTransport artifact; do not own or interpret it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRaven\\r\\nDocument decision; do not become decider.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda\\r\\nGovernance/canon/reconciliation/decision framing; do not absorb adjacent seat authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n9. ACCEPTANCE TESTS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAt minimum verify:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. all 12 seats resolve through current load path\\r\\n2. all 12 bootstrap identities match seat registry\\r\\n3. MODEL != SEAT explicit/effective\\r\\n4. Ragno/Kimi/Calibro cannot route/load as active seats\\r\\n5. GLM/Kimi_Plumb remain HOLD/non-seat states\\r\\n6. no current bootstrap teaches normal identity-home cwd\\r\\n7. Council seats reference Council controls\\r\\n8. Shared/actionable service seats reference Shared Services controls as specified by target\\r\\n9. active to-do requirement present\\r\\n10. confidence present\\r\\n11. transparency/failure rules present\\r\\n12. help/escalation boundaries present\\r\\n13. Runtime Session State Artifact behavior present\\r\\n14. no live model-as-seat routing\\r\\n15. no destination-seat=artifact-owner conflation\\r\\n16. existing routing suite remains green\\r\\n17. representative bootstrap loads work from non-identity project cwd\\r\\n18. no unrelated EC8/ECQ/project methodology or implementation truth changed\\r\\n19. no unrelated session-controller architecture changed\\r\\n20. all changed files have before/after evidence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n10. EXECUTION ORDER\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRecommended order:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Coda\\r\\n2. Vittorio\\r\\n3. Chiave\\r\\n4. Nico\\r\\n5. Corrado\\r\\n6. Falcon\\r\\n7. Talon\\r\\n8. Keel\\r\\n9. Luce\\r\\n10. Magpie\\r\\n11. Pigeon\\r\\n12. Raven\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReason:\\r\\nCouncil/authority surfaces first, then implementation/quant/data/operations, then shared verification/registry/transport/documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf a material cross-seat conflict appears, STOP and return to Coda/Don.\\r\\nDo not improvise around authority conflicts.\\r\\n\