ome first-class**, because right now Intent + Objective are explicit but hypothesis is mostly implicit.\n\n## What exists now\n\nThe parent is:\n\n**`GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25`**\n\nIts hierarchy is already:\n\n```text\nSESSION FRAME V3\n│\n├── Header\n│   ├── Don Intent Snapshot\n│   └── Active Context Board\n│\n├── Mid-Flight Frame\n│\n├── Checkpoint Frame\n│\n└── Footer\n    └── Routing / Handoff Appendix\n```\n\nAnd underneath that we now have class-specific controls:\n\n```text\nExecutive Council\n├── SESSION HEADER V1\n└── SESSION FOOTER V1\n\nShared Services\n├── SESSION HEADER V1\n└── SESSION FOOTER V1\n```\n\nplus the normalized:\n\n**`GCE_RUNTIME_SESSION_STATE_ARTIFACT_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25`**\n\n---\n\n# Where Intent + Objective are already strong\n\n### Session Frame V3 header\n\nIt already has:\n\n```text\nRAW INTENT:\n<what Don is actually saying/requesting>\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n<the concrete outcome Don is trying to achieve>\n\nCONTEXT:\n<why this matters / surrounding constraint>\n```\n\nSo the interpretive layer is already there.\n\nThe rule is also exactly right:\n\n> Don Intent Snapshot is interpretive, not authoritative.  \n> If Don corrects it, update immediately.\n\nThat is important because tonight showed why.\n\n---\n\n# Executive Council header is even better\n\nIt currently has:\n\n```text\nRAW INTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nWHY / CONTEXT\nINTENT CONFIDENCE\n```\n\nThen separately:\n\n```text\nCURRENT QUESTION\nCURRENT POSITION\nKNOWN\nUNKNOWN\nCONFLICT\nASSUMPTIONS IN USE\nAUTHORITY BOUNDARY\n```\n\nAnd then a **drift baseline**:\n\n```text\nBASELINE INTENT\nCURRENT INTENT\nMATERIAL CHANGE SINCE BASELINE\nDRIFT STATUS\n```\n\nThat is already very close to what you’re describing.\n\n---\n\n# Shared Services header\n\nFor Luce/Falcon/Magpie/etc., it currently uses:\n\n```text\nDON / REQUESTER INTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nSCOPE\nOUT OF SCOPE\nACCEPTANCE CONDITION\nINTENT CONFIDENCE\n```\n\nThat’s excellent for bounded execution.\n\nIt answers:\n\n> What was I asked to do?  \n> What observable thing proves I’m done?\n\n---\n\n# The Footer is already doing the important close\n\nThis is the part you were remembering.\n\nThe **Executive Council Footer** explicitly contains:\n\n```text\nENTRY INTENT\nENTRY OBJECTIVE\n\nEXIT OBJECTIVE STATE:\nACHIEVED | PARTIAL | BLOCKED | CHANGED | SUPERSEDED\n\nCURRENT INTENT AT EXIT\nCURRENT OBJECTIVE AT EXIT\n\nINTENT / OBJECTIVE DELTA\nDRIFT STATUS\n```\n\nThat is exactly the mechanism that should have caught our issue tonight.\n\nIf:\n\n```text\nOBJECTIVE:\nDon can operate normally\n```\n\nand we proved:\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS 1:\nInternet is the problem\n\nRESULT:\nFALSE\n```\n\nwe are **not done**, because:\n\n```text\nEXIT OBJECTIVE STATE != ACHIEVED\n```\n\nThat’s your point.\n\n---\n\n# Runtime State Artifact\n\nThis is also already strong.\n\nIt requires every material state write to restate:\n\n```text\nINTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nCURRENT_TASK\nCURRENT_STATE\nACTIVE_TODO\nSCOPE\nNEXT_ACTION\nEXIT / STOP CONDITION\n```\n\nAnd importantly:\n\n> Intent and objective must be restated explicitly rather than inherited implicitly.\n\nThat’s already designed specifically for drift detection.\n\n---\n\n# What is missing\n\nThere is **no explicit first-class HYPOTHESIS lifecycle**.\n\nRight now hypotheses get buried inside:\n\n- `CURRENT QUESTION`\n- `ASSUMPTIONS IN USE`\n- `KNOWN / UNKNOWN`\n- active to-do items\n- investigative prose\n\nThat’s why a seat can accidentally behave as though disproving the user's proposed cause means the job is complete.\n\nWe need this distinction mechanically visible:\n\n```text\nOBJECTIVE\nWhat state are we trying to produce?\n\nINTENT\nWhy / what are we fundamentally trying to accomplish?\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nWhat explanation or route are we testing right now?\n```\n\nAnd then:\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS STATUS:\nUNTESTED | TESTING | SUPPORTED | REJECTED | INCONCLUSIVE\n\nEVIDENCE:\n<what proved/disproved it>\n\nOBJECTIVE IMPACT:\nACHIEVED | STILL OPEN | CHANGED\n```\n