--\n\n# 5. ROUTING / BUS MAP\n\nLuce identified the actual topology clearly. fileciteturn0file0L181-L199\n\n### LIVE\n\n**Canonical handoff bus**\n\n`GCE_ORG\\...\\Operations\\06_HANDOFFS\\<Seat>\\`\n\nKeep.\n\n---\n\n**DevPad / VoiceBridge transport**\n\n`GCE_DON\\command-center\\ai-inbox\\`\n\nKeep the bus.\n\nRemove **model addressing as an allowed producer contract**.\n\n---\n\n**Cable Car outbound**\n\n`GCE_DON\\06_OUTBOX`\n\nKeep.\n\n---\n\n### DORMANT\n\n`GCE_DON\\mailroom`\n\nDo not resurrect in this pass.\n\n---\n\n### DEAD / HISTORICAL\n\n`GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS`\n\nArchive later.\n\n---\n\n### D-4 CODA RULING — MODEL-NAMED ROUTES\n\n`kimi`, `glm`, and `claude` are **not valid destination seats**.\n\nTherefore:\n\n> **No new traffic may be generated into model-addressed lanes.**\n\nBut **do not blindly delete the directories** because Luce found pending messages and live VoiceBridge/inbox consumers.\n\nNico should:\n\n1. disable creation of new model-addressed messages;\n2. remove model-address buttons/tool choices from live producer surfaces;\n3. mark legacy lanes **DEPRECATED / DRAIN ONLY**;\n4. leave existing payloads untouched;\n5. require legacy messages to be explicitly re-addressed to a valid seat rather than silently forwarding them.\n\n**No `Kimi → Vittorio`, `GLM → Chiave`, etc. automatic aliasing.**\n\nThat would recreate `MODEL == routing identity` indirectly.\n\n---\n\n# 6. PROJECT OWNERSHIP MAP\n\n### Framework\n\n**Authority:** `GCE_ORG`\n\n`GCE_DON\\GCE_Framework` is stale residue, not the live Framework authority.\n\n---\n\n### EC8 / Edge Crew Quant\n\nCurrent implementation truth remains primarily:\n\n`GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant`\n\nThere remains a **known dual-root condition** involving `Desktop\\mlb-data-system` and an additional preserved quant implementation. Luce explicitly could not establish the relationship between those implementations. fileciteturn0file0L223-L248\n\n**Do not touch EC8 in this pass.**\n\n---\n\n### DevPad / Command Center\n\nCurrent runtime:\n\n`GCE_DON\\command-center`\n\nOld EdgeCrew DevPad copies are historical.\n\n---\n\n### VoiceBridge\n\nCurrent truth:\n\n`GCE_DON\\voice-bridge`\n\n---\n\n### Cable Car\n\nCurrent truth:\n\n`GCE_DON\\command-center\\cable-car`\n\n---\n\n# 7. IDENTITY POLLUTION — CAUSE VS RESIDUE\n\nThis is one of Luce's strongest findings.\n\n### Mechanism\n\n**FIXED.**\n\nDevPad now starts seats in runtime roots rather than identity cwd and actively rejects accidental identity cwd. fileciteturn0file0L253-L266\n\n### Doctrine\n\n**NOT FIXED.**\n\nEleven bootstrap files still instruct the operator to enter:\n\n`GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>`\n\nas the workspace root.\n\nThat instruction can still create new work product there.\n\n### Residue\n\nVerified current residue:\n\n- Luce: 44 non-identity files.\n- Talon: 29.\n- Falcon: 6.\n\nThere are also two real dependencies blocking a blind cleanup: Talon identity files referenced from `opencode.json`, and a Luce PowerShell capture script that writes into the identity tree. fileciteturn0file0L268-L278\n\n### D-5 CODA RULING\n\nYour ownership doctrine resolves this:\n\n> **GCE_IDENTITY = seat identity and load control. It is not a working-project filesystem.**\n\nTherefore the canonical loading doctrine becomes:\n\n> **Load the seat from the active workspace/project root using the router/load command. Never change cwd to GCE_IDENTITY merely to acquire identity.**\n\nExisting identity residue is **not moved in this pass**.\n\nFirst stop new pollution.\n\nThen reconcile/migrate residue separately.\n\n---\n\n# 8. CABLE CAR CURRENT STATE\n\nCable Car is substantially healthy.\n\nThe contract now supports:\n\n- project metadata;\n- workstream metadata;\n- separated seat/authority attribution;\n- routing metadata;\n- explicit `owns_artifact:false`;\n- 1.0 compatibility;\n- registry parity tests.\n\nIts contract suite is 151/151 green. fileciteturn0file0L282-L296\n\n### Real current defect\n\nCommitted transport config accepts:\n\n`1.0`\n\nonly.\n\nThe corrected contract shape includes `1.1`.\n\nTherefore a valid 1.1 envelope can fail Drive inbound before schema validation even begins.\n\n### Secondary config residue\n\n`DRIVE_*_TEST` committed placeholder IDs remain in real-mode configuration.\n\nThe environment currently masks this, but committed configuration is misleading.\n\n### Current state\n\n**Cable Car = functional transport infrastructure with one real version-gate defect and minor config residue.**\n\nNo redesign required.\n\n---\n\n# 9. KEEP\n\nKeep intact:\n\n- `seat_registry.json`\n- router registry/footer/state modules\n- routing test suite\n- `GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md`\n- storage taxonomy freeze\n- `06_HANDOFFS`\n- `04_PROJECTS` pointer-layer concept\n- universal bootstrap T0/T1/T2 model\n- `UNSET` convention\n- current Cable Car contract architecture\n- current DevPad runtime-root mechanism\n- existing SUPERSEDED banners\n- `GCE_DON\\99_ARCHIVE` as live provenance\n\n---\n\n# 10. FIX NOW\n\nThe one-pass implementation should correct:\n\n1. Ragno retirement across every live authority/consumer.\n2. stale GCE_ORG canonical banners.\n3. stale Calibro redirect in locked bootstrap schema.\n4. `GCE_DON\\AGENTS.md`.\n5. Cable Car 1.1 gate.\n6. Cable Car synthetic committed folder IDs.\n7. stale seat-to-retired-seat routing prose.\n8. model-as-seat / model-as-canonical language.\n9. identity cwd bootstrap doctrine.\n10. model-address production in VoiceBridge/ai-inbox.\n11. missing Calibro retirement marker.\n12. explicit `model_not_equal_seat:true`.\n13. obvious dangling project pointers.\n\n---\n\n# 11. FIX LATER\n\nNot part of the one-pass:\n\n- migrating the 79 identity-residue files;\n- ECQ dual-root reconciliation;\n- de-overloading frozen `06_HANDOFFS`;\n- pruning 78 empty GCE_ORG directories;\n- moving old EC8 evidence;\n- Desktop Luce telemetry disposition;\n- dead-floor cleanup;\n- mailroom normalization;\n- broad deduplication.\n\n---\n\n# 12. SUPERSEDE\n\nSupersede, don't erase:\n\n- `GCE_ORG\\README.md`\n- `GCE_ORG\\02_COUNCILS\\README-CANONICAL.md`\n- old technical-strategy council manifest\n- stale EdgeCrew methodology README\n- old Framework handoff DOCX\n- stale roster/operator portion of `GCE_DON\\AGENTS.md`\n\nAlso surgically supersede the **Calibro redirect statement** inside the otherwise-current universal bootstrap schema.\n\n---\n\n# 13. ARCHIVE\n\nEligible **later**, not during this Nico pass:\n\n- historical `GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS`\n- old EdgeCrew DevPad\n- historical ECQuant handoff ZIP after consumer check\n- Talon `council_identity` history after dependency removal\n- verified duplicate datasets/handoffs/maps\n\nDo **not** archive `GCE_DON\\99_ARCHIVE`; Luce verified that live bootstraps reference it as provenance. fileciteturn0file0L319-L330\n\n---\n\n# 14. UNKNOWN\n\nRemain genuinely unknown and untouched:\n\n- whether Drive consumed all outbound files;\n- exact content class of the 171 KB `c6-verify` evidence JSON;\n- relationship between the multiple ECQ implementations;\n- intent of Vittorio mailroom directory shape;\n- writer/consumer of Desktop Luce telemetry.\n\nThese do **not** block the bounded taxonomy repair.\n\n---\n\n# 15. DON / CODA DECISIONS ACTUALLY REQUIRED\n\nLuce proposed five decisions. fileciteturn0file0L397-L436\n\nUnder the current handoff, all five are now resolved:\n\n| ID | Ruling |\n|---|---|\n| **D-1 Ragno** | **RETIRED.** Current Don authority overrides stale registry state. |\n| **D-2 Canon** | `seat_registry.json` is singular roster machine authority. Old prose canon becomes SUPERSEDED + pointer. |\n| **D-3 Calibro** | **RETIRED.** Remove the supposed live `Calibro → Nico` redirect. Nico is addressed directly. |\n| **D-4 Model lanes** | **DEPRECATED / DRAIN ONLY.** No new model-address traffic. No automatic model→seat forwarding. |\n| **D-5 Identity cwd** | **PROHIBITED AS NORMAL LOAD DOCTRINE.** Identity is load/control state, not project workspace. |\n\n### Therefore\n\n**No further Don ruling is necessary before implementation.**\n\nIf implementation exposes a new contradiction not contained in Luce's evidence, Nico surfaces it rather than inventing a resolution.\n\n---\n\n# 16. ONE-PASS NICO IMPLEMENTATION PACKAGE\n\nThis is the package.\n\n**Do it once. Then Luce verifies it once.**\n\n| # | Exact defect | Exact path/component | Exact desired state | Dependency | Risk | Required test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **N1** | Ragno remains live in machine roster | `seat_registry.json`, `GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md`, Cable Car contract enums, relevant bootstraps/aliases | Ragno moved to retired; aliases removed from active routing; no loadable Ragno destination | none — Don ruling now explicit | **MED** because multiple parity-linked surfaces | Routing 41/41 + Cable Car 151/151; Ragno must return `SEAT_RETIRED` |\n| **N2** | Stale 09-02 prose claims canonical roster | `GCE_ORG\\README.md`, `02_COUNCILS\\README-CANONICAL.md`, technical-strategy manifest, EdgeCrew methodology README | prominent `SUPERSEDED` banner + pointer to registry/router; preserve historical body | N1 so pointer lands on final roster | LOW | search live/current canon surfaces for unsupported Kimi/Big Pickle seat claims |\n| **N3** | LOCKED schema says `Calibro → Nico` redirect remains live | `UNIVERSAL_BOOTSTRAP_SCHEMA.md:146-147` | mark redirect retired; direct routing to Nico only; retain provenance note | none | MED because document is authority-bearing | routing tests + exact grep: no active Calibro forwarding claim |\n| **N4** | Root `GCE_DON\\AGENTS.md` is stale and bootstrap-like | `GCE_DON\\AGENTS.md` + registry deny roots | NON-AUTHORITY/SUPERSEDED banner; pointer to registry/router; add to bootstrap deny set | N1/N3 | LOW | `isDeniedBootstrapPath` test + routing parity |\n| **N5** | Cable Car inbound rejects corrected schema 1.1 | `command-center\\cable-car\\config\\cable_car.json` | supported versions = `1.0`,`1.1`; configured current version coherent with validator | none | LOW | add 1.1 inbound fixture; all existing 151 tests remain green |\n| **N6** | Real-mode config contains synthetic `DRIVE_*_TEST` IDs | same config | committed placeholders null/neutral; actual folder resolution remains env/runtime driven; fail loudly without required env | none | LOW | missing-root negative test + normal transport tests |\n| **N7** | Live bootstraps route through retired/model identities | Coda, Keel, Pigeon, Chiave and any other verified occurrences | route only to valid seats; delete retired/model destination semantics | N1/N3 | MED | grep all loadable AGENTS files for active `Kimi`, `Calibro`, `GLM` route directives |\n| **N8** | Ragno remains referenced as active/on-demand | Luce, Nico, Vittorio, project bootstrap reference specifically identified by Luce | retired/history wording only; no routable/on-demand Ragno | N1 | LOW | repository search + router rejection test |\n| **N9** | Models presented as canonical seat identity | Falcon, Raven, Magpie and matching live bootstrap text | occupant/model recorded only as occupancy; never identity/canon | none | LOW | grep for `canonical: DeepSeek`, `Big-Pickle` identity language |\n| **N10** | Bootstrap schema key absent | every canonical loadable `GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>\\AGENTS.md` | explicit `model_not_equal_seat: true`; normalize YAML blocks where applicable without changing seat responsibility | none | LOW | automated bootstrap conformance test |\n| **N11** | Bootstraps teach cwd-in-identity | canonical seat bootstraps | replace with “load seat from active workspace/root”; GCE_IDENTITY is not working cwd | none | MED because this changes operator behavior | static test forbidding identity-cwd load instruction; launch 4 representative seats and inspect cwd |\n| **N12** | Live producer surfaces still create model-addressed traffic | VoiceBridge config/code, ai-inbox README/tool surface | disable KIMI/GLM/CLAUDE as new destinations; legacy folders `DEPRECATED/DRAIN ONLY`; no automatic forwarding | preserve existing messages | MED because VoiceBridge/inbox are live | VoiceBridge 35/35 + send tests valid-seat succeeds/model-address rejects |\n| **N13** | Calibro handoff folder lacks retirement marker | `06_HANDOFFS\\Calibro\\RETIRED-SEAT.md` | mirror Kimi retirement-marker pattern; historical artifacts preserved | none | NONE | corpus audit remains 9 known pre-existing violations |\n| **N14** | Three project pointers point to nonexistent roots | `04_PROJECTS` pointer READMEs identified by Luce | update only where destination is verified; otherwise mark unresolved/absent—never invent target | verified target path | LOW | filesystem existence check |\n| **N15** | Stale root authorization surface still mentions obsolete Big Pickle shell authority | `ROOT_AUTHORIZATION_REGISTRY.md` | mark pending/stale clause as superseded or remove obsolete authorization only after verifying zero live consumer | machine consumer check | MED | search consumers first; routing + command-center tests afterward |\n\n## Nico boundaries\n\n**DO NOT:**\n\n- move EC8;\n- reconcile ECQ dual roots;\n- bulk-move identity residue;\n- touch Drive contents;\n- restructure `06_HANDOFFS`;\n- rebuild routing;\n- resurrect Mailroom;\n- implement carousel/controller;\n- touch quant semantics;\n- perform archive cleanup;\n- create another recon package.\n\n### Acceptance gate\n\nAfter Nico finishes:\n\n1. `node --test routing/test/*.test.js` → **all green**\n2. Cable Car suite → **all green**\n3. Cable Car contract corpus → **same known pre-existing count unless intentionally corrected**\n4. VoiceBridge tests → **all green**\n5. explicit negative routing:\n   - Ragno rejected as retired\n   - Kimi rejected as model/retired identity\n   - Calibro rejected\n   - GLM cannot become destination seat\n6. seat bootstraps load from non-identity workspace\n7. no current canon surface presents Big Pickle, Kimi, GLM, Calibro, or Ragno as an active seat\n8. no new producer can create model-addressed ai-inbox traffic\n\n---\n\n## CODA DISPOSITION\n\n**Current-state reconciliation: COMPLETE.**\n\n**Architecture rewrite required:** NO.  \n**Additional recon required:** NO.  \n**Don decision gate remaining:** NO.  \n**Ready for Nico:** **YES.**\n\nLuce's original package stopped because the evidence showed genuine authority conflicts. fileciteturn0file0L440-L460 Those conflicts are now resolved by the current Don-authority handoff.\n\nThe next flow is therefore exactly:\n\n**Coda reconciliation → Nico one-pass implementation → Luce verification → continue.**\n\nNo extra slice in between."]}, "create_time": 1790381625.54867, "end_turn": true, "id": "eb825fd1-e524-41de-b76c-a7027146ce3d", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 814, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "62e5665f-6e41-4c3e-aa16-84451d078ea7", "cited_message_idx": 22, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_768b5812333c8191a39e2a55d3998273", "line_range": [22, 44], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_000000006ec08230a635fe694335df44", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "## A. EXECUTIVE CURRENT STATE\n### What is actually healthy (VERIFIED)\nThe **routing substrate is real, enforced, and green.** This is not a paper design.", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 785}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 1432, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "62e5665f-6e41-4c3e-aa16-84451d078ea7", "cited_message_idx": 22, "cloud_doc_url": 