ce Bunny and Nex. memcite\n\nSo the clean direction is:\n\n> **Main DevPad = stable/current work.**  \n> **Rookie DevPad = alternate-model audition / overflow board.**\n\nI would not hard-code a permanent “pirate crew” mapping yet. We had explicitly avoided making Rookie a fixed seat→model board; the transport envelope should identify project/workstream + desired seat, while runtime/provider/model stays swappable. memcite\n\nIf you want the **first-pass Rookie lineup** based on what we actually tested/discussed, I’d load it like this:\n\n| Seat function | Rookie occupant candidate |\n|---|---|\n| Coda | alternate strategic model / open audition |\n| Chiave | alternate architecture model / open audition |\n| Vittorio | Space Bunny |\n| Nico | **Nex N2.5 Pro** |\n| Luce | Space Bunny |\n| Talon | MiMo / Dots audition |\n| Keel | Space Bunny / Nex depending build load |\n| Falcon | Ling / Dots |\n| Corrado | keep specialty-only; model audition only when quant work exists |\n\nThat is **candidate state**, not frozen doctrine. The only one with a stronger prior performance signal from Black Pearl/DevPad testing was **Nex N2.5 Pro for Nico-type implementation**, with Space Bunny also proving useful in execution/verification lanes. memcite\n\nAnd importantly: the **Rookie DevPad was discussed/spec’d, but not actually built yet**. The Main DevPad seat changes were implemented; Rookie was still the next surface to create. memcite\n\nIf you want, next I can give you the **exact Rookie DevPad build prompt for Nico** — bounded to “clone the board mechanics, separate state, AD HOC banner, alternate model mappings, no impact to Main.”"]}, "create_time": 1790386994.276328, "end_turn": true, "id": "b4c42609-c145-4a1e-a724-85e34863ed0b", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 553, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 544, "type": "