ND not durable handoff evidence\nAND not retired-lane provenance\n```\n\nIf any clause fails: **HOLD**.\n\nThat makes cleanup mechanical instead of interpretive.\n\n---\n\n## What I would call the work item\n\n**GCE DRIVE / CABLE CAR ACCESS & LIFECYCLE HARDENING**\n\nThis should be its own Framework infrastructure pass, separate from the Rookie build.\n\nThe target outcome is not “fix one bug.” It is:\n\n> Any seat, in any session, gets the same answer to:\n> **How do I access Drive? What is authoritative? What does each transport surface mean? What can I clear? What constitutes a completed transfer?**\n\nAnd yes — I would fix this **before we let Rookie depend heavily on Drive**, because otherwise we are about to multiply the same ambiguity across a second DevPad.\n\nIf you want, I can now turn the two evidence sets you gave me into **one proper Coda → Nico implementation package** for this system-wide hardening pass."]}, "create_time": 1790398409.70742, "end_turn": true, "id": "1652aee4-0fd1-4c81-98f9-4af1cf2442c7", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "aeai4r", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "t1sq1n", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "abc01241-6eea-41d6-b512-07a3f68cb097", "request_id": "8614e287-70ac-4f68-947d-d65b18036bc6", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "64be5319-f7d2-4e48-8f43-a42105eff2bd", "working_turn_id": "64be5319-f7d2-4e48-8f43-a42105eff2bd"}, "recipient": "al